## Original Content
This week's episode of the Modern Retail Podcast features a conversation with Once Upon a Farm Chief Marketing Officer Katie Marston about how the company has sought to shake up the baby aisle with coolers. Marston shares what she's learned over the years about what it takes to get retailers on board with a new way of merchandising products.

## Summary
Once Upon a Farm is innovating in the baby aisle by introducing coolers for product merchandising, as discussed by CMO Katie Marston on the Modern Retail Podcast. The company is shaking up traditional retail methods to get retailers on board with new ways of presenting baby products. This approach highlights the challenges and strategies in retail innovation for baby food and related items.

## Key Points
- Once Upon a Farm is using coolers to innovate how baby products are merchandised in retail aisles.
- Katie Marston, the CMO, shared insights on the strategies required to convince retailers to adopt new merchandising techniques.
- The discussion took place on the Modern Retail Podcast, focusing on practical steps for retail disruption.
- The company aims to transform the traditional baby aisle experience through product preservation and display methods.


